    "name": "ACME Salary Management API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Built from the uploaded Express source. Covers all 8 implemented method/path combinations.\n\nSETUP: Start your backend and seed its currencies. Set collection variable baseUrl to your server origin (default http://localhost:3000, without trailing slash). No authentication middleware is present in the supplied source.\n\nRUN: Run the entire collection in order with one iteration. Create employee generates a unique code/email and saves employeeId. Salary requests use that ID. Running creates one persistent test employee and one salary change; there is no delete endpoint. Re-running the whole collection creates a fresh employee. For individual salary requests, first run Create employee or set employeeId yourself; exact history-count checks assume the ordered fresh-employee workflow.\n\nMONEY: salaryMinorUnits is a positive integer, not a formatted amount. INR/USD/GBP use 100 minor units per major unit; JPY uses 1. 5000000 INR = INR 50,000. Insights are expressed in USD minor units. No salary period is assumed.\n\nFILTERS: country IN/US/GB/JP; department Engineering/Finance/HR/Sales; level Junior/Mid/Senior/Lead. page >= 1; pageSize 1..100. Strict schemas reject unknown body/query keys. Currency codes must also exist in the database.\n\nVerification: generated from source and checked for JSON and script syntax; not executed against a running API/database."
  },
